  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="7e58bade-544f-5183-a421-129543d3f0cb" activityNameId="89dca8f9-e843-54e3-aa6e-9770e29993dc" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xxx Door, inner, glass-wood, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xxx Door, inner, glass-wood, at plant
The dataset can be applied to describe an average room door. The door frame is made of massive wood, the door leaf is made of wood with a glass insert (62 % wood, 38% glass). The lock, door handles and frame joints are fabricated from steel. Data are based on a door of 0.8x2.0 m and scaled to 1m2. 1 m2 of the wooden inner door weighs 27.6 kg. The functional life time for the door frame is 50 years, for the door leaf it is 30 years. \nGeography: Data from producers in Switzerland.\nTechnology: The technology represents average European production.\nVersion: 2.2\nEnergy values: Undefined\nLocal category: Bauteile\nLocal subcategory: Türen\nUVEK 2022 source file:07154.XML\n\n
UUID: 803af2c7-5f58-377f-95fc-e461084c9ff9
This dataset describes the production of 1m2 (visible area) inner door, including the processes for the installation. Not included are transports from plant to construction site.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: The technology represents average European production.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Published study, Internet search 
Extrapolations: see Geography
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_803af2c7-5f58-377f-95fc-e461084c9ff9.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
